.PP 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim, template< uint32_t > class functor, class real> \fBNewtonRaphsonSolve0\fP< dim, functor, real >\fB::NewtonRaphsonSolve0\fP (real X0, real Epsilon, bool Twice_df, unsigned int max_iter, functor< dim > & F, real(functor< dim >::* f )(real), real(functor< dim >::* df )(real), real(functor< dim >::* d2f )(real) = \fRNULL\fP, real fsolve = \fR0\fP, bool check_boundary = \fRfalse\fP, real min_x = \fR0\fP, real max_x = \fR0\fP)\fR [inline]\fP"
This constructor sets everything needed by the algorithm\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIX0\fP This is the starting point of the search\&. It is stored as the data member, _x0\&. 
.br
\fIEpsilon\fP The is used to define the end point of the iterative procedure, do_iteration\&. The loop will terminate when the abs(F(xi) - fsolve)) is less than Epsilon\&. It is stored as the data member, _epsilon\&. 
.br
\fITwice_df\fP If Twice_df then the derivative of F, at point i, is approximated as (F(x[i])+f(x[i-1])*\&.5 which approximates the derivative of F over the interval x[i] to x[i-1]\&. It is stored as the data member, _F\&. 
.br
\fImax_iter\fP The maximum number of iterations before do_iteration, will terminate\&. It is stored as the data member _max_iter\&. 
.br
\fIF\fP This reference to a functor object serves as the object for calling the member function pointers f, df and d2f\&. It is stored as the data member _F\&. 
.br
\fIf\fP This pointer to a member function is used to calculate the function to solved\&. It is stored as the data member _f\&. 
.br
\fIdf\fP This pointer to a member function is used to calculate the derivative of the function to solved\&. It is stored as the data member _df\&. 
.br
\fId2f\fP This pointer to a member function is used to calculate the second derivative of the function to solved\&. It is stored as the data member _d2f\&. 
.br
\fIfsolve\fP This is the value of f to be solved\&. It's default value is 0\&. It is stored as the data member _fsolve\&. 
.br
\fIcheck_boundary\fP If true then the algorithm will check constrain the search so that it only stays within min_x and max_x\&. If the search goes outside of the range then the solution is set to the boundary value\&. It is stored as the data member _check_boundary\&. 
.RE
